# Parriwimple, Bildrath's nephew (docs/voice/parriwimple.md)

~ start
if flag.parriwimple_befriended
Parriwimple [smile]: Hello again. I remembered you. I don't remember everybody.
else
Narrator: A very large young man is stacking sacks of flour into a perfect pyramid, counting under his breath. He stops at forty-one and looks down at you, pleased.
Parriwimple: Hello. Uncle says to say welcome. Welcome.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* What are you counting? -> counting
* What's the pastry woman like? -> pie_lady
* [if flag.burial_agreed and not flag.parriwimple_pallbearer and not flag.burgomaster_buried] Could you help carry the burgomaster's coffin? -> coffin
* [if not flag.parriwimple_befriended] Say something kind to him. -> befriend
* [if flag.parriwimple_befriended and not flag.parriwimple_book_shown] What do you do at night, when the shop is shut? -> book
* [if tarokka.ally.npc == parriwimple and not guest:parriwimple] Madam Eva's cards named you, Parriwimple. Come with us. -> ally
* Goodbye. -> END

~ counting
Parriwimple: Days. Since the burgomaster died. Three. Nobody else counted, I think. Somebody should.
interject tag:veteran: Somebody should. Good man.
-> menu

~ pie_lady
set bonegrinder_rumor
Parriwimple: The pie lady. Uncle won't let me eat them; he says they cost money. She lives in the old windmill on the Vallaki road. I carried sacks there once. It smelled like bread. And like not bread.
interject tag:curious: Not bread? What does "not bread" smell like?
Parriwimple: I didn't like it. I carried the sacks fast.
-> menu

~ coffin
if flag.parriwimple_befriended
set parriwimple_pallbearer
Parriwimple [smile]: I can carry that. I'll bring the shovel too, and dig. Uncle won't mind. Uncle will mind. I'll go anyway.
else
Parriwimple: Uncle says my time costs money. Five gold an hour. You'd have to ask Uncle. He likes being asked.
endif
-> menu

~ book
Parriwimple: At night, when Uncle bolts the shutters and goes up the stairs, I take the big book down from the desk.
Parriwimple [sly]: Uncle thinks I only know the numbers on the sacks. I can read. I read his book.
Parriwimple: The big book has everyone in the village in it, and beside every name is what they took home without paying.
Parriwimple: Goodwife Viorica owes for salt since the winter before last, and Old Florin owes for three yards of wool.
Parriwimple [weary]: Nobody has paid a copper against the book in four years, and Uncle writes the new sums in every week.
Parriwimple: He never asks them for it when they come in. He only shouts about the price of rope so they look at the floor.
Parriwimple: Is it wicked, to keep a book of debts you never ask for? Or is that what kind looks like, when you're also frightened of waste?
* It's kind. -> book_kind
* It's bad business. -> book_business

~ book_kind
set parriwimple_book_shown
Parriwimple [smile]: I thought it might be kind. It feels heavy like kindness when I put it back on the shelf.
Parriwimple: Though if Uncle is a good man, I must be very careful not to let him find out.
Parriwimple [weary]: It would upset him terribly, and he has enough to oil and count as it is.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You told Parriwimple his uncle's book was kind
-> menu

~ book_business
set parriwimple_book_shown
Parriwimple: Yes. Uncle says it is ruinous business every night while he scrapes the mud off his boots.
Parriwimple: He says it very loud when the door is open, so the whole street hears that Bildrath is a hard man.
Parriwimple [sad]: I think if he did not say it was bad business out loud, he would have to say that everyone is hungry.
-> menu

~ befriend
* [Persuasion DC 10] You're good at this, Parriwimple. Your uncle's lucky to have you. -> befriend_ok | befriend_fail
* [Wizard] Show him a little magic. -> befriend_magic
* Never mind. -> menu

~ befriend_ok
set parriwimple_befriended
Parriwimple [smile]: Nobody says that. Uncle says I'm a good lifter. That's nearly the same. Thank you. I'll remember you.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 wren_featherfoot +1 kip_smudgewick +1: You were kind to Parriwimple
-> menu

~ befriend_fail
Parriwimple: Thank you? I think? Uncle says people say nice things when they want a discount. There's no discount.
-> menu

~ befriend_magic
set parriwimple_befriended
Narrator: A spark, a puff of colored light, a floating flour-dust star. Parriwimple watches it with his whole face.
Parriwimple [smile]: Again. No. Don't, Uncle will charge you for the flour. But that was the best thing I ever saw. I'll remember you.
inspire class:wizard: made a flour-dust star for Parriwimple
approve ratatoille +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You showed Parriwimple a little magic
-> menu

~ ally
Parriwimple: Me? In the cards? Nobody ever saw me in anything before.
Narrator: He sets down a sack of flour, very gently, as if it might wake.
Parriwimple: Uncle says I'm not to leave the shop. Uncle says a lot. I can carry your packs. I can carry you, if you fall down. I'll count the days we're gone so he knows.
interject tag:kind: You'll do more than carry, Parriwimple.
join parriwimple
-> END

~ graveside
Parriwimple: The grave's ready. I put the dirt in a neat pile, so it goes back in neat. Uncle says neat is respect.
* Thank you, Parriwimple. Let's begin. -> village_of_barovia/burial:start
* Not yet. -> END
